<title>USA: High Plains Wheat - Scattered new crop protection.</title>
<headline>High Plains Wheat - Scattered new crop protection.</headline>
<dateline>KANSAS CITY, Mo. 1997-03-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>There was scattered two to four cents per bushel protection posted on new crop wheat in Kansas and Oklahoma Monday and isolated four to five cents on old crop wheat, grain merchandisers said.</p>
<p>Protection was taken ahead of an expected lower opening on KCBT new crop futures on spillover selling from an anticipated sharp drop in CBOT new crop soybeans on bearish acreage data issued earlier Monday by the U.S. Department of Agriculture.</p>
<p>One Kansas dealer reported heavy farmer selling of new crop wheat but other merchandisers said trade was slow.  </p>
